      "id": 1,
      "text": "Cushman began in 1886 as a railroad terminus after a construction accident on the Iron Mountain line, quickly becoming a key shipping hub for the Batesville Manganese District.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        21
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://grokipedia.com/page/cushman_arkansas"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "Manganese mining powered Cushman’s boom, employing up to 900 Italian workers in 1918 to meet wartime steel demands.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        3
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://grokipedia.com/page/cushman_arkansas"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "In 1956, the film Come Next Spring was shot in a fictionalized version of Cushman, giving the town a brief Hollywood spotlight.",
